error[E0401]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), so it must be used exactly once, but `twice` may use it more than once
 --> usage.ck:5:10
  |
5 | fn twice f : f~File
  |          ^
  = help: a resource can't be copied; thread it with `<-` so each use gets the new one

error[E0401]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), so it must be used exactly once, but `never` never uses it
 --> usage.ck:9:10
  |
9 | fn never f -> n : f~File, n~Nat
  |          ^
  = help: close it, or pass it on

error[E0402]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), but `one_branch` uses it on some paths and not on others
  --> usage.ck:12:15
   |
12 | fn one_branch f b : f~File, b~Bool
   |               ^
   = help: a resource must be used exactly once on every path, e.g. closed in every branch

error[E0403]: `src` is `ghost`: it may only appear in types and constraints, but `ghostly` uses it at runtime
  --> usage.ck:19:12
